# Houdini preparation contract audit (3 October 2026)

## Are existing records sufficient after origins disappear? (3 October 2026)

- Current.json preserves projectId, loadId, workspace path, verifiedAt and files containing id, path, sha256 and the exact backup record. Backup contains sourceId, relativePath, size, sha256, manifestPath, sourceFolder and relativeManifest. Thus the file identity and archived version survive deletion of the production file. (3 October 2026)
- The real zenray-assets-v2 Current.json inspected here contains one restored file; its productionBaselines has 22 entries, each carrying only changeToken and sha256. These are actual structural observations, not proof that real production Houdini scenes were LOADed in this audit. Newly created workspace files may be inventoried without appearing in the original Current.json; rely on their verified state.backups/restorations when appropriate. (3 October 2026)
- Current.json alone lacks original source absolute paths and the scene reference graph. It must be joined with the stable project registry and retained scene audit. Registry sourceId -> localPath/namespace plus backup.relativePath reconstructs the declared original path without requiring that origin to exist. The new originCanonicalPath/relocation-required projection makes this relation explicit. (3 October 2026)
- productionBaselines is only a guard against an older unchanged original replacing newer cloud bytes. It is not an origin path table, resource graph, installed-library proof or fresh restored-byte proof. It should not become the new routing authority. (3 October 2026)
- A historical source path that was a symlink can have a different audited canonicalPath from source.localPath + relativePath. A deleted alias cannot be canonicalized afterward. Preserve an exact admitted origin alias when known, or report unresolved; do not guess by basename. Current service source admission rejects symlink redirection, reducing this issue for newly admitted sources. (3 October 2026)
- Public/cloud sceneReferences retains stable targets and parameter node paths but intentionally omits local raw/absolute paths. It is enough to select exact identities and plan local destinations; raw parameter expressions and origin canonical evidence must come from the retained local audit or a fresh headless audit. (3 October 2026)

## Minimum local preparation contract (3 October 2026)

- One scene identity, expected scene SHA256, verified loaded scene destination, and a list of verified resource identities are the inputs. Resource entries join target projectId/fileId to a managed restoration path, exact expected SHA256/size and original reference provenance. Shared library identity must belong to the declared dependency closure. This plan stays local; export only identities, relative paths, counts and diagnostics. (3 October 2026)
- Verify that each chosen path remains a regular file inside its admitted active LOAD root, contains no symlink escape, and has exact expected bytes before launching HOM. Current.json describes a past proof; it does not attest that the file has remained unchanged. Reuse existing descriptor/stability checks and archive verifier rather than trusting status=verified alone. (3 October 2026)
- First rebind scope: unambiguous mapped or relocation-required references with explicit input role, a static direct parameter, and a verified target. Dynamic expressions, channel/keyframe references, unknown roles, outputs, URI, relative search paths, directories and missing targets remain separate and untouched. A mapped unknown HDA with null parameterPath can be included in the separate library-install list after verifying it is an actual HDA definition file. (3 October 2026)
- The isolated hython session installs only those verified HDA files, loads the verified scene with manual update, applies eligible bindings in memory and evaluates their string paths. No .hip save is needed for this first proof; no original is changed. Missing-library load warnings are recorded and cannot be suppressed into success. The preparation may remain partial even if loading succeeds. (3 October 2026)
- Proof fields should distinguish sceneOpened, resourceBytesVerified, reboundInputs, loadedLibraries, unresolvedReferences and warnings. For each HDA instance, check the active definition library path points to the expected restored file; merely listing a library as installed does not prove the instance uses that definition. Rehash scene and resources afterward and preserve portabilityVerified=false because no complete cooking/render/game verification occurred. (3 October 2026)
- This in-memory preparation is a verifier and a foundation for a later managed launch operation. Ending hython discards the in-memory bindings. It does not by itself make a double-click on the unchanged .hiplc portable or persist a prepared user scene. Any later derived scene must be separately identified and preserved alongside the original archived bytes. (3 October 2026)

## Real HOM red/green test, isolated from production (3 October 2026)

- Build a disposable fixture source with a tiny explicit input parameter, one HDA instance and its external library, plus a directory reference/output that should not be rebound. Save only this fixture, archive/restore to a different managed root and retain its exact scene hash. The fixture is not Ceramic or Louisiana production. (3 October 2026)
- RED: hide or rename the disposable original resource root, load the identical restored scene, and assert original input is absent and HDA instance is incomplete or uses no approved restored definition. Also show that merely restoring bytes does not fix these facts. (3 October 2026)
- GREEN: install the restored HDA in the isolated session and rebind the known input to its restored path; assert parm.evalAsString equals the admitted loaded target, file bytes match, and node.type().definition().libraryFilePath resolves to the restored HDA. No cook/render required for this narrow resolution proof. (3 October 2026)
- Negative variants: modified restored bytes, missing dependency, ambiguous identity, stale scene hash, redirected symlink, expression/channel-bound parameter, invalid HDA and unknown output role. The first five block preparation; the latter unsupported references stay explicit rather than being rewritten or claimed validated. Then rehash original/loaded fixture scenes to prove no save. (3 October 2026)

## Official primitive references (3 October 2026)

- [hou.hipFile](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/hom/hou/hipFile.html) supplies load and explicit load warnings; setName changes only session naming and save is a distinct operation. (3 October 2026)
- [hou.hda](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/hom/hou/hda.html) supplies definitionsInFile and session library installation; use change_oplibraries_file=False, with explicit definition selection verified afterward. It need not modify user OPlibraries. (3 October 2026)
- [hou.Parm](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/hom/hou/Parm.html) explains that set follows channel references by default. The first preparation must admit only direct static parameters, rather than breaking expressions or modifying their referenced controllers. (3 October 2026)

- Only this dated read-only audit deliverable was written. No rendering, production scene load/save, source modification, shared code change, skill change or commit. (3 October 2026)
